heritageGraph:FearlessnessAssessment a owl:Class,
        linkml:ClassDefinition ;
    rdfs:label "FearlessnessAssessment" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf heritageGraph:RitualAssessment ;
    skos:definition "The 'fearlessness test' popularly described (animal heads, masked dancers in darkness). Its historical and contemporary practice is DISPUTED -- some former Kumaris contest how it is described. Represented as an assessment whose accounts are source-attributed via has_assertion, NOT as a mandatory criterion." ;
    skos:exactMatch heritageGraph:FearlessnessAssessment ;
    skos:inScheme heritageGraph:schema ;
    skos:scopeNote "Deliberately not a SelectionCriterion subclass: popular accounts and lived testimony disagree. Attach each account as a Assertion (CRMinf I2 Belief) with its own source and confidence." .

